  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building Opportunities and Outcomes in Social Protection and Youth Employment</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of the Building Opportunities and Outcomes in Social Protection and Youth Employment Project for Somalia is to enhance economic opportunities and strengthen the resilience of the poor and vulnerable. There are three components to the project, the first component being connecting youth and women to better jobs today. This component will support 28,000 youth (60 percent women and 5 percent people living with disability) to access wage and self-employment activities, contributing directly to inclusive job creation and strengthening households resilience to shocks. The second component is investing in people for better jobs tomorrow. This component forms the cornerstone of the project&apos;s direct support to poor and vulnerable households by integrating social protection with human capital development, climate adaptation and resilience, and future job readiness. Utilizing a multisectoral approach for best outcomes, the component aims to tackle multiple dimensions of poverty and climate vulnerability, combining resilient support for the poorest households with co-responsibility transfers aimed at improving specific human capital outcomes in health, nutrition, and education, which are essential foundations for future labor force participation and economic inclusion. This component includes two subcomponents: unconditional cash transfers and human capital co-responsibility cash transfers. Finally, the third component is the adaptive social protection systems and project management. This component supports three key areas crucial for the long-term sustainability and effectiveness of social protection interventions in Somalia and Somaliland. This component includes three subcomponents: adaptive social protection systems, national socio-economic survey, and project management.</narrative>
  </description>
